  "description": "EVO PDF Library for .NET (Classic) can be used in .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard applications on Windows to convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG, create and edit PDF documents. It can also merge, split, stamp, secure and fill existing PDF documents.\n\nThis metapackage references the EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf package.\n\nThe same EvoPdf API runs on the Chromium-based engine of EvoPdf Next, on Windows, Linux and macOS, in the EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf.Windows, EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf.Linux, EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.HtmlToPdf.MacOS packages: an application keeps its code and changes only the package reference.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, on x64 and ARM64, EvoPdf Next offers a newer Chromium-based rendering engine for modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript in the multi-platform package EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf and in the platform packages EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.MacOS.\n\nThe full EvoPdf Next library, which also converts Word, Excel, RTF and Markdown to PDF, comes in the EvoPdf.Next, EvoPdf.Next.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nMigration guide from Classic to Next:\nhttps://www.evopdf.com/evopdf-classic-to-next-migration\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML with CSS3, SVG, web fonts and JavaScript to PDF\n* Create PDF links, forms, bookmarks and table of contents from HTML\n* Place HTML content in PDF pages, headers and footers\n* Convert HTML to JPEG, PNG and SVG images\n* Create PDF documents with text, graphics and images\n* Set PDF security and digital signatures\n* Edit, stamp, merge and split PDF documents",
